Recommends: wtype | xdotool
Description: Modern clipboard manager for Linux (Wayland & X11)
 Clypse is a fast, native clipboard manager built with Rust, GTK4 and
 libadwaita. It uses the zwlr-data-control-v1 Wayland protocol for
 event-driven clipboard monitoring without polling.
 .
 Features:
  - Persistent SQLite history with FTS5 full-text search
  - Favorites system — starred items are never auto-deleted
  - Real-time clipboard capture via Wayland wlr-data-control protocol
  - Native GTK4/libadwaita UI following GNOME/COSMIC HIG
  - systemd user service with sd_notify(READY=1) integration
  - Hash-based deduplication — no duplicate entries
